The model contract is now fixed: recent-window log trend for participation with a persistence baseline; ridge-style linear composition forecasts constrained back to the probability simplex; and attribute-only score regression mapped to difficulty tertiles, with chronological holdouts throughout. The sensitivity and falsification checks will explicitly test window choice, shuffled word attributes, non-five-letter exclusion, and rounding normalization.
